    "model_details": "economy_potential",
    "model_description": "Continues from max_map_action_space (the \"Easyish\" level-0..5 model) with reworked reward mechanics (\"scheme 3\"). Shaping is emitted per action; the end-turn step emits none; after opponents move, the baseline absorbs only ownership changes while the economy term (4*farms - trees on the agent's land) is preserved as a continuous potential. This closes a reward-farming hole (being paid to re-clear free tree regrowth) and adds direct signals to keep the tree population down and to protect farms (losing a farm scores -4*income_weight on the next step, without double-counting the hex). income_weight is raised so economy is competitive with territory. Goal: aggressive early expansion plus economy upkeep, to beat level 5 on merit.",
